WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.680 align:start position:19%
On a Tuesday evening in August 2011 in a
rented rehearsal space above a noodle

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:12.040 align:start position:19%
shop in To Kwa Wan, a 60-year-old man
picked up a guitar. He was jamming with

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:15.800 align:start position:19%
friends, amateur stuff, cover songs for
nobody. Halfway through a song, his left

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.440 align:start position:19%
hand stopped moving. Then his legs gave
out. His skull hit a concrete stairway

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.120 align:start position:19%
on the way down and split open a 5-in
gash above his left ear. By the time an

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.600 align:start position:19%
ambulance arrived, the right side of his
body was already dead. The man on that

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.560 align:start position:19%
floor was Gordon Liu. He had played the
most iconic Shaolin monk in cinema

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:34.160 align:start position:19%
history. He had been Quentin Tarantino's
white eyebrow killing master in Kill

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.720 align:start position:19%
Bill. His face had been sampled,
referenced, and worshipped by the

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:42.120 align:start position:19%
Wu-Tang Clan for two decades, and he was
about to disappear into a wheelchair, a

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:46.720 align:start position:19%
courtroom, and a silence that has now
lasted longer than his entire film

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:51.400 align:start position:19%
career. His real name was Sin Kwok Wah,
born in Foshan, Guangdong province in

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:55.920 align:start position:19%
1951, the same city that produced Wong
Fei Hung, the most mythologized martial

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.400 align:start position:19%
artist in Chinese history. That is not a
coincidence. It is the whole story. His

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.560 align:start position:19%
family moved to Hong Kong when he was a
child. His father sold antiques and arts

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.960 align:start position:19%
and crafts exports out of a shop in
Sheung Wan. The household was

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.560 align:start position:19%
comfortable. Gordon was the youngest of
four children, spoiled and undisciplined

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.320 align:start position:19%
by his own later admission. His parents
wanted nothing to do with martial arts.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.480 align:start position:19%
They feared it would turn him into a
street fighter. He started training

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.840 align:start position:19%
anyway. Around age seven, he began
sneaking off to a Hung Gar school run by

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:24.760 align:start position:19%
a man named Lau Cham. Lau Cham was not a
random Sifu. He was a direct student of

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.425 align:start position:19%
Lam Sai Wing, who was the senior
disciple of Wong Fei Hung himself. That

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.800 align:start position:19%
makes the lineage four generations
[music] deep. Wong Fei Hung to Lam Sai

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:38.360 align:start position:19%
Wing to Lau Cham to the kid from Sheung
Wan who kept cutting school. Between 15

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.360 align:start position:19%
and 20, Gordon skipped classes almost
daily to train. Hung Gar tradition

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.800 align:start position:19%
demanded up to three years of nothing
but stance work before you learned a

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.920 align:start position:19%
single technique. Gordon did three years
of stance work. By night, he taught

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:54.480 align:start position:19%
classes at Lau Cham's school. By day, he
worked as a shipping clerk. Lau Cham's

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.440 align:start position:19%
wife encouraged him to take the family
surname. He became Lau Kar Fai, in the

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.440 align:start position:19%
West, Gordon Liu. [music] He was not
adopted, he was not Lau Cham's son, he

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.080 align:start position:19%
was his godson. That distinction
matters. Nobody chose him by default, he

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.800 align:start position:19%
chose the lineage and the lineage
accepted him. Lau Cham had two

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:14.280 align:start position:19%
biological sons already working in film.
The elder was Lau Kar-leung, a top

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.760 align:start position:19%
action choreographer at Shaw Brothers
Studios. The younger was Lau Kar-wing.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:22.120 align:start position:19%
Gordon became their godbrother and Lau
Kar-leung was about to become the most

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:26.480 align:start position:19%
important director he would ever work
with. Shaw Brothers Studios in the

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:30.360 align:start position:19%
mid-1970s was a factory. They shot on
permanent backlot sets at Movie Town in

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:34.240 align:start position:19%
Clearwater Bay. They produced dozens of
martial arts films a year and they had

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:38.520 align:start position:19%
just promoted Lau Kar-leung from
choreographer to director. His first

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:43.800 align:start position:19%
lead actor was Gordon Liu. The film was
Challenge of the Masters in 1976. Gordon

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:47.440 align:start position:19%
played Wong Fei-hung, the folk hero his
own godfathers lineage had trained

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:51.440 align:start position:19%
under. A real lineage descendant playing
the ancestor on screen. Nobody in the

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:55.560 align:start position:19%
audience knew that, but Lau Kar-leung
knew it. He built the next decade of his

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:59.440 align:start position:19%
career around Gordon's body. Over the
following 12 years they made roughly 19

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:04.480 align:start position:19%
films together. Executioners from
Shaolin, Heroes of the East, Dirty Ho,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:08.560 align:start position:19%
My Young Auntie, Martial Club, [music]
Legendary Weapons of China. All four

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:12.840 align:start position:19%
screenplays Lau ever wrote, starred or
featured Gordon Liu. No director star

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:18.120 align:start position:19%
partnership in kung fu cinema was more
prolific and in 1978 they made the one

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:22.560 align:start position:19%
that changed everything. The 36th
Chamber of Shaolin was not the biggest

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.720 align:start position:19%
grossing Shaw Brothers film. It earned
close to 3 million Hong Kong dollars

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:30.959 align:start position:19%
domestically, but it did something no
kung fu film had done before. It spent

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:34.959 align:start position:19%
more than 45 minutes inside a training
sequence. Gordon plays Liu Yu-de, a

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.239 align:start position:19%
young student whose family is killed by
Manchu soldiers.

00:03:36.152 --> 00:03:40.400 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; He flees to the Shaolin Temple, he

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:44.360 align:start position:19%
shaves his head and then chamber by
chamber he earns his way through 35

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.320 align:start position:19%
stages of physical and mental
discipline. Wrist strengthening with a

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:52.320 align:start position:19%
stone-tipped rod, balance drills on
floating logs, headbutting sandbags

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.200 align:start position:19%
until his skull bleeds. [music] A pole
striking gauntlet that plays like a

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.960 align:start position:19%
full-body percussion exam. Each chamber
has its own logic, its own failure

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.480 align:start position:19%
condition, [music]
its own moment of breakthrough. The

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:07.200 align:start position:19%
training sequence is the movie. Gordon
carries every frame of it alone. No

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:10.800 align:start position:19%
sidekick, no love interest, no comic
relief until the final act. He plays the

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.000 align:start position:19%
same character at three ages and makes
each one physically distinct. The young

00:04:12.832 --> 00:04:19.160 align:start position:19%
[music] student is loose and panicked.
The mid-training monk is tense and

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:23.480 align:start position:19%
methodical. The graduated master San Te
moves like water finding its level. He

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.720 align:start position:19%
shaved his own head for real. That
image, bald skull in a yellow robe,

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:32.440 align:start position:19%
became the most recognizable silhouette
in kung fu cinema. It won Best Martial

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:36.280 align:start position:19%
Arts at the 24th Asian Film Festival.
American distributors retitled it Master

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:41.080 align:start position:19%
Killer and dumped it into grindhouse
theaters in 1979. One of those

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:44.840 align:start position:19%
grindhouse theaters was on 42nd Street
in Manhattan. A kid from Staten Island

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:48.840 align:start position:19%
named Robert Diggs saw it there when he
was about 14. [music] He had already

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:52.880 align:start position:19%
seen it once on Channel 5 at age 9. He
would eventually watch it roughly 300

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.960 align:start position:19%
times. He built an entire mythology
around it. He named his crew after

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:01.280 align:start position:19%
another Gordon Liu film. He called his
debut album Enter the Wu-Tang: 36

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:05.840 align:start position:19%
Chambers. The opening track samples a
line of dubbed English dialogue from

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:10.240 align:start position:19%
Shaolin and Wu-Tang, a 1983 film that
Gordon Liu directed himself. The line

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:15.000 align:start position:19%
about Shaolin shadowboxing and the
Wu-Tang sword style became one of the

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:20.400 align:start position:19%
most recognized audio samples in hip-hop
history. Robert Diggs became RZA. His

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:24.600 align:start position:19%
crew became the Wu-Tang Clan. And Gordon
Liu, the actor whose dubbed voice

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.400 align:start position:19%
launched the whole thing, never received
a credit, a royalty, or a phone call.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:33.080 align:start position:19%
The Wu-Tang Clan named their
neighborhood Shaolin. They named their

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:37.360 align:start position:19%
chambers, they named their styles, all
of it traced back to a Cantonese actor

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:42.120 align:start position:19%
working on a back lot in Clearwater Bay.
Gordon Liu's face is on bootleg t-shirts

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:46.720 align:start position:19%
in every Chinatown in America. His voice
opens one of the best-selling rap albums

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:50.080 align:start position:19%
of the 1990s, and almost nobody wearing
those shirts or playing that album could

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:55.640 align:start position:19%
tell you his [music] name. That Then
came July 7th, 1983. Alexander Fu Sheng,

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:59.760 align:start position:19%
Shaw Brothers biggest young star, died
in a car accident. He had been the lead

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:03.840 align:start position:19%
of a film still in production called The
Eight-Diagram Pole Fighter. Lau

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:08.280 align:start position:19%
Kar-leung rewrote the script overnight.
Gordon Liu's character, Fifth Brother

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:11.720 align:start position:19%
Yang, became [music] the protagonist.
There was a scene in that film where

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:15.600 align:start position:19%
Gordon shaves his head on camera. It was
always in the script, but after Fu

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:20.080 align:start position:19%
Sheng's death, it became something else.
It became grief filmed in real time. The

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:24.200 align:start position:19%
Eight-Diagram Pole Fighter is widely
considered Lau Kar-leung's darkest and

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:28.000 align:start position:19%
most brutal film. It was also the last
great martial arts picture Shaw Brothers

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:33.000 align:start position:19%
ever produced. The studio stopped making
films in 1986, and when the factory

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.200 align:start position:19%
closed, Gordon Liu had no factory.
Jackie Chan had already gone

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:39.720 align:start position:19%
international. Jet Li was rising fast on
the mainland. Sammo Hung and Yuen Biao

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:44.720 align:start position:19%
were building their own production
pipelines. Gordon Liu signed with TVB

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:48.880 align:start position:19%
and spent the 1990s doing television,
police procedurals, supporting comedic

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:53.160 align:start position:19%
roles, steady work that nobody outside
Hong Kong ever saw. In 1993, a film

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:56.800 align:start position:19%
called Last Hero in China put him on a
rope bridge opposite Jet Li. The scene

00:06:55.040 --> 00:07:00.480 align:start position:19%
plays like a passing of the torch,
old-school Hung Gar against new-school

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:04.800 align:start position:19%
wushu, the bald Shaw monk against the
rising mainland idol. The fight is good,

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:08.919 align:start position:19%
the metaphor is brutal. That same year,
Lau Kar-leung was hired to choreograph

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:12.000 align:start position:19%
Jackie Chan's Drunken Master II. The two
men [music] clashed over fight

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:15.760 align:start position:19%
philosophy so severely that Lau walked
off the production before the final

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:20.360 align:start position:19%
fight was shot. Chan reshot it in his
own style. Lau responded by making

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:23.800 align:start position:19%
Drunken Master III with Gordon Liu. It
flopped, [music] a master and his

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:28.720 align:start position:19%
godbrother answering a slight with a box
office disaster. The 1990s were not

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:32.760 align:start position:19%
kind. Then, in 2002, a phone call came
from Los Angeles. Quentin Tarantino

00:07:30.919 --> 00:07:36.880 align:start position:19%
wanted Gordon Liu for a film called Kill
Bill. Liu later told CNN he had barely

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:42.040 align:start position:19%
heard of the director. His own words in
a 2007 interview captured the confusion

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:45.400 align:start position:19%
perfectly. He was a 1970s Asian star. He
could not understand why anyone would

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:49.080 align:start position:19%
want him in a 21st century American
film. They met in Shanghai. Gordon wore

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:52.960 align:start position:19%
a formal Chinese suit. [music]
Tarantino, to his surprise, wore one,

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:57.760 align:start position:19%
too. The first word Tarantino said to
him was Shifu, master. For volume one,

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:01.920 align:start position:19%
Gordon played Johnny Mo, the masked
leader of the Crazy 88. Tarantino had

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:06.000 align:start position:19%
him kill and be killed in the most
elaborately choreographed sword fight in

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:10.000 align:start position:19%
American film history. For volume two,
something stranger happened. Tarantino

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:13.400 align:start position:19%
had originally cast himself as Pai Mei,
the white-eyebrowed Shaolin villain. He

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:17.520 align:start position:19%
trained for the role. He put on the
costume. He started shooting. Gordon Liu

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:21.240 align:start position:19%
watched him in the makeup chair and told
him to his face that he looked like

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:24.840 align:start position:19%
Santa Claus, not a martial arts master.
Tarantino has confirmed the story. He

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:27.640 align:start position:19%
said, "It seemed like a big pain to play
the character and he wanted to

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:31.919 align:start position:19%
concentrate on directing." He said
having Gordon Liu in the wings made the

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:36.640 align:start position:19%
decision easy. He called it almost
criminal not to cast him. The Pai Mei

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:41.385 align:start position:19%
that ended up on screen, stroking his
beard, flicking his wrist, humiliating

00:08:39.159 --> 00:08:44.320 align:start position:19%
Uma Thurman with a contemptuous grin,
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:48.160 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; was Gordon Liu's creation. The
beard-stroking gesture was his idea. It

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:53.640 align:start position:19%
was not in the script. And here is the
detail that makes it ache. In

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:57.480 align:start position:19%
Executioners from Shaolin, made in 1977,
Gordon Liu played the hero who fights

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:01.720 align:start position:19%
Pai Mei. 26 years later, he became the
villain he once tried to kill. Kill Bill

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:06.200 align:start position:19%
made Pai Mei iconic. It did not make
Gordon Liu a star. He returned to Hong

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:10.760 align:start position:19%
Kong. He did a Bollywood crossover film
in 2009 called Chandni Chowk to China,

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:15.160 align:start position:19%
playing a smuggler villain opposite
Akshay Kumar for Warner Brothers. He

00:09:12.839 --> 00:09:18.760 align:start position:19%
attended a documentary premiere in Rome.
He reunited with Lau Kar-leung for a

00:09:16.839 --> 00:09:23.680 align:start position:19%
final collaboration. And he kept playing
guitar with friends in a rented room in

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:26.839 align:start position:19%
Tokwawan until August 2011, when a
stroke dropped him on a staircase and

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:30.360 align:start position:19%
opened a wound that has never fully
closed. The paralysis took his right

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:34.800 align:start position:19%
side. The speech impairment took his
voice. Within 18 months, he had lost

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:39.200 align:start position:19%
nearly 50 lb. Visitors to the hospital
found a man who could nod, shake his

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:42.880 align:start position:19%
head, and move his left arm. That was
it. When a reporter asked if he was

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:46.680 align:start position:19%
happy, he nodded. When a visitor's
zipper was down, Gordon spotted it

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:51.160 align:start position:19%
immediately and tried to gesture. Sharp
mind, locked body. His second wife, Ma

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:54.760 align:start position:19%
Fei Fung, and their two children were
estranged by then. Tabloid reports

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:58.840 align:start position:19%
alleged they had pried open floorboards
in his Cane Road apartment searching for

00:09:56.440 --> 00:10:02.040 align:start position:19%
hidden cash. Ma denied it publicly,
saying the floors were being repaired

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:06.640 align:start position:19%
for mold damage. Gordon filed for
divorce in June 2012. He entrusted his

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:11.880 align:start position:19%
remaining liquid assets, roughly 2
million RMB plus a US dollar account, to

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:15.680 align:start position:19%
his assistant of 5 years, a woman named
Eva Fung. By December 2012, the money

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:19.680 align:start position:19%
was gone and Eva was not returning
calls. Gordon Liu could not speak, could

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:23.800 align:start position:19%
not walk, and could not get his own
savings back. His elder sister Teresa,

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:27.520 align:start position:19%
living in the United States, arranged
for actress Amy Fan, a long-time friend,

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:32.520 align:start position:19%
to take over as legal guardian in
January 2013. Amy paid for lawyers out

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:36.440 align:start position:19%
of her own pocket. She hired a private
nurse. She moved Gordon into a nursing

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:40.400 align:start position:19%
home. And she went after Eva Fung in
court. Eva initially refused even to

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:44.160 align:start position:19%
accept the subpoena. The confrontation
reportedly ended with Amy Fan shouting

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:47.520 align:start position:19%
at her outside a building demanding she
take the paper threatening to call

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:55.280 align:start position:19%
police. Eva took it. The Bank of China
account showed 1.39 million RMB. The

00:10:50.839 --> 00:11:00.200 align:start position:19%
HSBC account showed 58,000 US dollars.
On April 29th, 2014, 1 day before the

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:05.560 align:start position:19%
High Court hearing, Eva agreed to return
approximately 1.2 million RMB plus

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:09.160 align:start position:19%
interest. Gordon Liu, the man who had
played the most disciplined monk in

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.640 align:start position:19%
cinema, the most terrifying master in
Tarantino's universe, got most of his

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:16.560 align:start position:19%
money back through a last-minute
settlement negotiated by a television

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:21.400 align:start position:19%
actress and funded by her personal
savings. Two months before that

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:26.040 align:start position:19%
settlement, on June 25th, 2013, Lau
Kar-leung died at Union Hospital in Hong

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:29.839 align:start position:19%
Kong. He was 76. Lymphoma had stalked
him for two decades. When Amy Fan told

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.120 align:start position:19%
Gordon the news, his eyes went red. He
did not speak. He

00:11:31.032 --> 00:11:35.640 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; never speaks when he is unhappy. The man

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:41.400 align:start position:19%
who made him, who named him, who [music]
pointed a camera at him 19 times and

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:45.520 align:start position:19%
built the most important kung fu film
ever shot around his body was gone.

00:11:43.478 --> 00:11:50.360 align:start position:19%
[music] And Gordon could not say goodbye
out loud. In 2020, the Martial Arts

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:54.560 align:start position:19%
History Museum inducted him into its
Hall of Fame. In February 2025, he

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:58.320 align:start position:19%
appeared at the Hong Kong Stunt Men
Association's New Year dinner in a

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:02.280 align:start position:19%
wheelchair, receiving a contribution
award. It was his first significant

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:05.400 align:start position:19%
public appearance in years. He is 73
years old. He lives in a Hong Kong

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:10.480 align:start position:19%
nursing home under Amy Fan's
guardianship. He does not give

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:14.720 align:start position:19%
interviews. He has not acted since 2011.
The paradox of Gordon Liu is simple to

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:18.000 align:start position:19%
state and impossible to resolve. His
image is everywhere. His bald head in

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:21.680 align:start position:19%
that yellow robe is printed on shirts
sold in cities he has never visited. His

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:26.640 align:start position:19%
dubbed voice opens one of the most
important albums in hip hop. His white

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:30.400 align:start position:19%
eyebrows and contemptuous grin define
one of Tarantino's most quoted

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:34.320 align:start position:19%
characters. Hundreds of millions of
people have consumed his work. Almost

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:39.240 align:start position:19%
none of them know his name. Bruce Lee
died young and became a god. Jackie Chan

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:42.880 align:start position:19%
survived and became a brand. Gordon Liu
survived and became a sample. He is

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:47.480 align:start position:19%
sitting in a nursing home in Hong Kong
right now. A fourth generation inheritor

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:51.880 align:start position:19%
of Wong Fei Hung's kung fu, the monk,
the master, the man whose voice built a

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:56.600 align:start position:19%
mythology he was never invited into.
Still sharp behind the eyes. Still

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:56.600 align:start position:19%
silent.

